                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what is meant by \"rainbows devoid of color.\" This phrase does not make sense because rainbows are inherently colorful. So, the statement is false.\n\nSecondly, the concept of yin and yang colors is rooted in traditional Chinese philosophy and refers to the balance of opposing forces. It is not related to the formation of rainbows.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) False.",
