                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the concept of yin and yang colors.\nYin and yang are concepts from Chinese philosophy that represent the duality of nature, with yin being the passive, dark, and feminine aspect, and yang being the active, bright, and masculine aspect.\n\nStep 2: Understand the concept of rainbows.\nRainbows are meteorological phenomena that occur when sunlight is refracted, reflected, and dispersed through water droplets in the air, resulting in a spectrum of colors appearing in the sky.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the relationship between yin and yang colors and rainbows.\nRainbows are created by the dispersion of light, not by the mixing of yin and yang colors. The colors in a rainbow are a result of the natural properties of light and the way it interacts with water droplets in the atmosphere.\n\nConclusion: Rainbows are not devoid of color made by mixing yin and yang colors.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
