                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: Would a Beaver's teeth rival that of a Smilodon?\n\nProfessor: Well, let's think about this. What are some of the differences between beavers and Smilodons?\n\nStudent: Well, Smilodons are a lot bigger, for one.\n\nProfessor: That's true, Smilodons are much larger animals. But size isn't everything. Let's look at the teeth. What do you notice about a beaver's teeth?\n\nStudent: They're really sharp!\n\nProfessor: That's right, they're very sharp. And they're also very thick. So, if we compare the thickness of a beaver's teeth to the thickness of a Smilodon's teeth, what do you think we'll find?\n\nStudent: The beaver's teeth are thicker.\n\nProfessor: That's right, the beaver's teeth are actually thicker than the Smilodon's teeth. And that's why a beaver's teeth can rival that of a Smilodon.",
