                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) False\n\nExplanation:\n\nA beaver's teeth are not as large or as sharp as those of a Smilodon, which is an extinct species of saber-toothed cat. The Smilodon had large, curved canine teeth that were up to 7 inches long and were used to hunt and kill large prey. In comparison, a beaver's teeth are much smaller and are used for gnawing on wood and other materials. The beaver's incisors are only about 1 inch long and are not as sharp as those of the Smilodon. Therefore, a beaver's teeth would not rival that of a Smilodon and the answer is False.",
