                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Is consuming kidney safe?\nA) True\nB) False\n\nTo determine if eating kidney is safe, we need to consider factors such as the source of the kidney, proper preparation, and potential health risks.\n\n1. Source of the kidney: If the kidney comes from a healthy animal that has been raised and slaughtered under hygienic conditions, it is generally safe to eat. However, if the animal was sick or the kidney is contaminated, it could pose a risk.\n\n2. Proper preparation: Kidneys need to be cleaned and cooked properly to ensure they are safe to eat. This includes removing any visible fat and connective tissue, soaking the kidney in cold water to remove impurities, and cooking it thoroughly to kill any potential bacteria or parasites.\n\n3. Potential health risks: Kidneys are high in purines, which can be harmful to people with gout or kidney problems. Additionally, some people may have an allergic reaction to organ meats like kidneys. It is essential to be aware of any personal health issues or allergies before consuming kidney.\n\nConsidering these factors, we can conclude that:\n\nA) True - Eating kidney can be safe if it comes from a healthy source, is prepared correctly, and does not pose any personal health risks.",
