                    {
                        "id": "f3eed81c-0811-4f93-8024-c301aca5481e",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the properties of Mercury and the requirements for a good Slip N Slide material.\n\nMercury is a heavy, silvery-white liquid metal that is also known as quicksilver. It is a chemical element with the symbol Hg and atomic number 80. Mercury is the only metallic element that is liquid at standard conditions for temperature and pressure. It is used in various applications such as thermometers, barometers, and fluorescent lamps.\n\nA Slip N Slide is a recreational activity that involves sliding on a smooth, wet surface, usually made of plastic. The ideal material for a Slip N Slide should be:\n1. Slippery when wet\n2. Durable and able to withstand the weight and friction of people sliding on it\n3. Safe for human contact\n4. Easy to clean and maintain\n5. Environmentally friendly\n\nNow, let's evaluate Mercury based on these criteria:\n\n1. Slippery when wet: Mercury is a liquid metal, so it might provide a slippery surface. However, its high surface tension could make it less slippery than water or other lubricants typically used for Slip N Slides.\n\n2. Durable: Mercury is a liquid, so it would not provide a solid surface for people to slide on. It would also be difficult to contain and maintain a consistent layer of Mercury on a sliding surface.\n\n3. Safe for human contact: Mercury is toxic and can be absorbed through the skin or inhaled as vapor. Prolonged exposure to Mercury can cause serious health problems, including damage to the nervous system, kidneys, and lungs. Using Mercury as a Slip N Slide material would pose significant health risks.\n\n4. Easy to clean and maintain: Mercury is difficult to clean up due to its liquid state and tendency to form small droplets. It would be challenging to remove Mercury from a Slip N Slide surface and the surrounding environment.\n\n5. Environmentally friendly: Mercury is a hazardous substance that can contaminate soil, water, and air. Using Mercury for a Slip N Slide would pose a significant environmental risk.\n\nBased on these criteria, we can conclude that Mercury does not make for good Slip N Slide material. Therefore, the answer is:\n\nB) False",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c680d87a-61ed-4858-885b-766aaa866880",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-yes-no",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "No.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 05:28:00",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
