                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question - The question is asking if embalmed bodies feel different at funerals compared to non-embalmed bodies.\n\nStep 2: Define embalming - Embalming is the process of preserving a dead body by treating it with chemicals to slow down decomposition.\n\nStep 3: Consider the effects of embalming on a body - Embalming involves draining the body of fluids and replacing them with preservative chemicals. This process can make the body feel firmer and less pliable than a non-embalmed body.\n\nStep 4: Compare embalmed bodies to non-embalmed bodies - Since embalming makes the body feel firmer and less pliable, it is reasonable to assume that embalmed bodies would feel different at funerals compared to non-embalmed bodies.\n\nStep 5: Choose the correct answer - Based on the information above, the correct answer is:\n\nA) True",
