                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nEmbalming is a process that is used to preserve dead bodies. The process involves replacing the blood and other fluids in the body with embalming fluid, which is a mixture of formaldehyde, methanol, and other chemicals. The purpose of embalming is to slow the decomposition of the body and to make the body more presentable for viewing.\n\nThe process of embalming does not change the way the body feels. The body will still feel the same as it did when the person was alive.\n\nB) False",
