                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Is the term \"Homer\" in baseball named after the poet Homer who wrote the Odyssey?\n\nStep 1: Understand the context of the term \"Homer\" in baseball.\nIn baseball, a \"Homer\" is short for \"home run,\" which is when a batter hits the ball and is able to run around all the bases and score without being tagged out.\n\nStep 2: Research the origin of the term \"Homer\" in baseball.\nThe term \"Homer\" in baseball is derived from the phrase \"home run.\" It is not named after the poet Homer who wrote the Odyssey.\n\nStep 3: Verify the answer.\nSince the term \"Homer\" in baseball is derived from the phrase \"home run\" and not named after the poet Homer, the answer is:\n\nB) False",
