                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nLet's rephrase the question to be sure we understood it correctly:\n\nCould a young Wizard of Oz Scarecrow have gotten Cerebral Palsy?\n\nA) True\nB) False\n\nOur understanding is that the question is asking if it is possible for the Scarecrow character from the Wizard of Oz to have gotten Cerebral Palsy. We will reason through this question step by step.\n\nFirst, let's consider what Cerebral Palsy is. Cerebral Palsy is a neurological disorder that is caused by damage to the brain. This damage can occur before, during, or after birth.\n\nNow, let's think about the Scarecrow character. The Scarecrow is a fictional character, so we cannot know for sure if he could have gotten Cerebral Palsy. However, we can reason through this question by considering what we know about the character.\n\nThe Scarecrow is a character who is made out of straw. He does not have a real brain, so it is not possible for him to have gotten Cerebral Palsy.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the answer to the question is False. The Scarecrow character could not have gotten Cerebral Palsy.",
