                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the following factors:\n\n1. Temperature variations on Mercury\n2. Duration of day and night on Mercury\n3. Human adaptability to Mercury's environment\n\n1. Temperature variations on Mercury:\nMercury is the closest planet to the Sun, and its surface experiences extreme temperature variations. During the day, temperatures can reach up to 800\u00b0F (430\u00b0C), while at night, temperatures can drop to -290\u00b0F (-180\u00b0C). This means that warm weather attire would not be sufficient to protect against the extreme cold during the night.\n\n2. Duration of day and night on Mercury:\nA day on Mercury lasts about 59 Earth days, and a night on Mercury lasts about the same amount of time. This means that if a person were to stay on Mercury, they would experience extremely long periods of both extreme heat and extreme cold. Warm weather attire would not be suitable for such long durations of extreme cold.\n\n3. Human adaptability to Mercury's environment:\nMercury's environment is not suitable for human life without proper protection. The extreme temperatures, lack of atmosphere, and high levels of solar radiation make it impossible for humans to survive without specialized equipment and clothing. Warm weather attire would not provide the necessary protection against these harsh conditions.\n\nBased on these factors, the answer to the question is:\n\nB) False - Only warm weather attire would not be a good idea on Mercury, as it would not provide adequate protection against the extreme temperature variations and other harsh conditions present on the planet.",
                        "answers": [
