                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Light is the fastest known thing in the universe and travels at a speed of approximately 299,792,458 meters per second.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of a light year?\n2. How far does light travel in one year?\n3. Is a light year a measure of time or distance?\n4. What is the significance of a light year in astronomy?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A light year is a unit of measurement used in astronomy to describe the distance that light travels in one year.\n2. Light travels approximately 9.46 trillion kilometers (5.88 trillion miles) in one year.\n3. A light year is a measure of distance, not time.\n4. The use of light years in astronomy allows scientists to measure vast distances in space, such as the distance between stars and galaxies.",
