                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: A) the distance light travels in one year.\n\nExplanation: A light year is a unit of measurement used to measure astronomical distances. It is the distance that light can travel in one year, which is approximately 9.5 trillion kilometers (or 5.9 trillion miles). This is the equivalent of about 6 trillion miles per hour. Light travels at a constant speed, so the distance it travels in one year is the same regardless of the source of the light. Therefore, the answer is A) the distance light travels in one year.",
