                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.\n\nGravity plays a crucial role in the formation of stars. As clouds of gas and dust particles come together due to gravitational attraction, they begin to condense and form a dense core. As more and more matter accumulates in this core, the gravitational force becomes stronger, causing the core to collapse further. This collapse generates heat and pressure, which eventually triggers nuclear fusion and ignites the star. Therefore, option B is the correct answer as it describes the role of gravity in causing gases and dust particles to condense into spheres, which eventually form stars.",
