                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To rephrase the question: What is the role of gravity in the formation of stars?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\nA) Gravity converts solid matter into gases and light energy. - This statement is incorrect as gravity does not convert solid matter into gases and light energy.\n\nB) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres. - This statement is correct as gravity pulls gas and dust particles together, causing them to condense and form spheres.\n\nC) Gravity cools gases and liquids until they become one solid mass. - This statement is incorrect as gravity does not cool gases and liquids until they become one solid mass.\n\nD) Gravity pushes rocks and dust particles outward from a dense center. - This statement is incorrect as gravity pulls particles inward towards a dense center, rather than pushing them outward.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
