                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Read the question and the answer choices carefully.\n\nStep 2: Identify the keywords in the question. In this case, the keyword is \"gravity\" and \"formation of stars.\"\n\nStep 3: Go through each answer choice and eliminate the ones that are clearly incorrect.\n\nA) Gravity converts solid matter into gases and light energy. - This statement is incorrect as gravity does not convert solid matter into gases and light energy.\n\nB) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres. - This statement is a possibility as gravity can cause gases and dust particles to come together and form spheres.\n\nC) Gravity cools gases and liquids until they become one solid mass. - This statement is incorrect as gravity does not cool gases and liquids.\n\nD) Gravity pushes rocks and dust particles outward from a dense center. - This statement is incorrect as gravity pulls matter towards the center, not pushes it outward.\n\nStep 4: Compare the remaining answer choices and select the one that best describes the role of gravity in the formation of stars.\n\nB) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres. - This statement is the best description of the role of gravity in the formation of stars as it accurately describes how gravity pulls matter together to form stars.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
