                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking us to identify the statement that best describes the role of gravity in the formation of stars.\n\nStep 2: Review the answer choices\nA) Gravity converts solid matter into gases and light energy.\nB) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.\nC) Gravity cools gases and liquids until they become one solid mass.\nD) Gravity pushes rocks and dust particles outward from a dense center.\n\nStep 3: Recall information about star formation\nStars form from clouds of gas and dust in space. Gravity plays a crucial role in this process by pulling the gas and dust particles together, causing them to condense and form a dense core. As the core becomes denser, it heats up and eventually ignites nuclear fusion, creating a star.\n\nStep 4: Match the information to the answer choices\nThe information about star formation matches best with answer choice B, which states that gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.\n\nStep 5: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
