                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that stars form from clouds of gas and dust in space. These clouds are called nebulae. \n\nNext, we know that gravity plays a crucial role in the formation of stars. \n\nOption A is incorrect because gravity does not convert solid matter into gases and light energy. \n\nOption C is also incorrect because gravity does not cool gases and liquids until they become one solid mass. \n\nOption D is incorrect because gravity does not push rocks and dust particles outward from a dense center. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres. As the gas and dust particles come together, they begin to heat up due to the pressure and friction. Eventually, the temperature becomes so high that nuclear fusion occurs, and a star is born.",
