                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What is the role of gravity in the formation of stars?\nGravity plays a crucial role in the formation of stars. It is the force that pulls together the gas and dust particles in a cloud, causing them to condense and form a protostar.\n\nStep 2: Which statement best describes this role?\nA) Gravity converts solid matter into gases and light energy. - This statement is incorrect as gravity does not convert matter into gases and light energy.\nB) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres. - This statement is correct as gravity causes the gas and dust particles to come together and form a sphere.\nC) Gravity cools gases and liquids until they become one solid mass. - This statement is incorrect as gravity does not cool gases and liquids.\nD) Gravity pushes rocks and dust particles outward from a dense center. - This statement is incorrect as gravity pulls particles towards the center, not pushes them outward.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Gravity causes gases and dust particles to condense into spheres.",
