                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure which of these options best describes the Moon. Can you help me work through them?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's start with option A: \"Older than Earth.\" Do you know the approximate age of the Earth and the Moon?\n\nStudent: I think the Earth is around 4.5 billion years old, and the Moon is around 4.5 billion years old as well.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! The Moon is actually slightly younger than the Earth, having formed about 4.51 billion years ago, while the Earth is about 4.54 billion years old. So, option A is not the best description. Now, let's look at option B: \"Smaller than Earth.\" Do you know the relative sizes of the Earth and the Moon?\n\nStudent: Yes, the Earth is definitely larger than the Moon. I believe the Moon's diameter is about 1/4th that of Earth's.\n\nProfessor: Excellent! So, option B is a correct statement. But let's examine the other options to make sure we find the best description. Option C states that the Moon has the \"same climate as Earth.\" What do you know about the Moon's climate?\n\nStudent: Well, I know that the Moon doesn't have an atmosphere like Earth, so it doesn't have weather or water. Its temperature also varies greatly between day and night.\n\nProfessor: That's right! The Moon's climate is very different from Earth's due to its lack of atmosphere and extreme temperature variations. So, option C is not accurate. Finally, let's consider option D: \"Having the same atmosphere as Earth.\" You already mentioned that the Moon doesn't have an atmosphere like Earth. Can you elaborate on that?\n\nStudent: Sure, the Moon has a very thin atmosphere called an exosphere, which is not nearly as dense as Earth's atmosphere. It doesn't provide any protection from solar radiation or meteoroids like Earth's atmosphere does.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! So, option D is also not accurate. Based on our analysis, which option do you think best describes the Moon?\n\nStudent: I think option B, \"Smaller than Earth,\" is the best description of the Moon.\n\nProfessor: I agree! Well done working through each option to arrive at the correct answer.",
