                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the rock cycle\nThe rock cycle is a continuous process where rocks are formed, changed, and reformed through various processes such as weathering, erosion, heat, pressure, and cooling.\n\nStep 2: Identify the types of rocks\nThere are three main types of rocks: igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic. Each type of rock is formed through different processes in the rock cycle.\n\nStep 3: Understand how igneous rocks are formed\nIgneous rocks are formed when molten rock (magma) cools and solidifies. This can happen either below the Earth's surface (intrusive igneous rocks) or on the Earth's surface (extrusive igneous rocks) after a volcanic eruption.\n\nStep 4: Match the correct process to the formation of igneous rocks\nNow that we know igneous rocks are formed from the cooling and solidification of molten rock, we can match this process to the correct answer choice.\n\nAnswer: A) cooling temperatures",
