                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: What is the major process of surface rock formation on volcanoes?\n\nAnswer: A) Rock cools quickly from melted rock.\n\nExplanation: The major process of surface rock formation on volcanoes is when molten rock, or magma, cools quickly and solidifies. This process is known as extrusive igneous rock formation. The molten rock is expelled from the volcano and cools quickly when it comes into contact with the air. This process is different from other rock formation processes, such as sedimentary rock formation, which involves the deposition of sediment over time, or intrusive igneous rock formation, which involves the slow solidification of magma deep underground.",
