                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks after a layer of sediment is deposited on the ocean floor is B) burying. This is because as more layers of sediment accumulate on top of the initial layer, the weight and pressure from the overlying layers compress and compact the sediment. Over time, this compaction and cementation process turns the sediment into solid rock. Therefore, burying is the necessary step for the formation of sedimentary rocks. Heating, eroding, and weathering may occur at different stages in the rock cycle, but they are not the immediate next step after sediment deposition.",
                        "answers": [
