                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks after a layer of sediment is deposited on the ocean floor?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Sedimentary rocks are formed from the accumulation and cementation of sediment.\n- The first step is the deposition of sediment, which can happen in various environments, including the ocean floor.\n- After sediment is deposited, it can undergo different processes that lead to its transformation into sedimentary rock.\n- Heating (option A) is not typically a step in the formation of sedimentary rocks, as it is more relevant to metamorphic rocks.\n- Eroding (option C) is a process that happens before sediment is deposited, as it involves the breakdown and transportation of rock and soil.\n- Weathering (option D) is also a process that happens before sediment is deposited, as it involves the physical and chemical breakdown of rocks at the Earth's surface.\n- Burying (option B) is the most likely next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks, as it involves the gradual accumulation of more sediment on top of the initial layer, which can lead to compaction and cementation over time.\n\nAnswer: B) burying",
                        "answers": [
