                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's rephrase the question: What is the next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks after a layer of sediment is deposited on the ocean floor?\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step:\n\n1. Sediment is deposited on the ocean floor.\n2. The sediment is then buried by more sediment.\n3. The sediment is then subjected to pressure and heat, which causes it to become compacted and cemented together.\n4. The sediment is then eroded by wind and water, which breaks it down into smaller pieces.\n5. The sediment is then weathered by the elements, which further breaks it down into even smaller pieces.\n\nThird, let's make sure we have the right answer:\n\nThe correct answer is D) Weathering.",
