                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA) Burying\n\nThe formation of sedimentary rocks begins with the deposition of sediment on the ocean floor. This sediment is then buried by additional layers of sediment, which can occur over a long period of time. As the sediment is buried deeper and deeper, the pressure and temperature increase, leading to the next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks: heating. Heating causes the sediment to become lithified, or turned into rock. After lithification, the sedimentary rock can be subject to further processes such as erosion, weathering, and other geological processes.",
