                        "instruction": "refl-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "B) burying\n\nCritique: While heating, eroding, and weathering can all play a role in the formation of sedimentary rocks, burying is the most immediate and necessary step after sediment deposition. As more layers of sediment accumulate on top, the weight and pressure compress the lower layers, eventually forming solid rock.\n\nReconsidering other answer options:\nA) Heating: While heat can play a role in the formation of some sedimentary rocks (such as through the process of diagenesis), it is not the next step after sediment deposition.\nC) Eroding: Erosion is the opposite of sediment deposition and would not be the next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks.\nD) Weathering: Weathering is the breakdown of rocks into smaller pieces, which can then become sediment. It is not the next step after sediment deposition, but rather a precursor to it.\n\nFinal answer: B) burying",
                        "answers": [
                            {
