                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, a layer of sediment is deposited on the ocean floor. The next step in the formation of sedimentary rocks would be burying, as more layers of sediment accumulate on top of the initial layer. Over time, the weight of the overlying sediment compacts and cements the lower layers, forming sedimentary rock. Heating and weathering may occur later in the rock cycle, but they are not the immediate next step after sediment deposition. Erosion would actually be the opposite of sediment deposition and would not contribute to the formation of sedimentary rocks. Therefore, the correct answer is B) burying.",
