                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking about the effect of extensive glaciation on ocean ecosystems at the end of the Permian period, which is believed to have caused extinctions.\n\nStep 2: Recall the effects of glaciation on oceans\nGlaciation can cause a drop in sea level, which can affect ocean volume and area. It can also cause a drop in ocean salinity and density due to the addition of freshwater from melting glaciers. However, glaciation is not likely to increase exposure of oceans to ultraviolet radiation or tsunamis.\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer\nBased on the above information, the most likely effect of extensive glaciation on ocean ecosystems that could have caused extinctions is a steep drop in ocean salinity and density. Therefore, the correct answer is A) steep drop in ocean salinity and density.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e106cb8a-62f7-4f6f-ba56-376d0908f9d5",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
