                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Glaciation would involve the freezing of water, which would lead to a decrease in ocean salinity and density as the salt would be left behind in the remaining liquid water. This could disrupt ocean ecosystems.\n\nB) Glaciation would also lead to a decrease in ocean volume and area as water is locked up in ice. However, this would not necessarily have a direct impact on ocean ecosystems.\n\nC) Glaciation would not directly increase exposure of oceans to ultraviolet radiation, as ice would still block sunlight from reaching the water beneath.\n\nD) Glaciation would not directly increase exposure of tsunamis to ocean life, as tsunamis are caused by underwater earthquakes and other geological events, not ice.\n\nBased on this analysis, the most likely answer is A) steep drop in ocean salinity and density.",
