                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the characteristics of cold air at the tops of mountains.\n2. Determine how air flows in relation to pressure.\n3. Determine the density of cold air compared to warmer air.\n4. Determine if cold air at the tops of mountains is free of oxygen atoms.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Cold air at the tops of mountains is denser than warm air and tends to sink.\n2. Air flows from areas of high pressure to areas of low pressure.\n3. Cold air is denser than warm air, so it will sink and flow towards areas of lower pressure.\n4. Cold air at the tops of mountains is not free of oxygen atoms.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) will flow toward areas of lower pressure in valleys.",
