                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) is considered to be less dense than warmer air.\n\nWhen air is cold, its molecules move slower and are closer together, making the air more dense. However, when cold air is at the tops of mountains, it is at a higher altitude where the atmospheric pressure is lower. This lower pressure causes the cold air to expand and become less dense than the warmer air at lower altitudes. Therefore, option C is the correct answer. Option A is incorrect because air flows from areas of high pressure to areas of low pressure. Option B is incorrect because the cold air at higher altitudes is already at a higher pressure than the warmer air at lower altitudes. Option D is incorrect because the presence of oxygen atoms in the air is not related to its temperature or altitude.",
