                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Weathering is the process of breaking down rocks, soils, and minerals through natural processes. It can be physical, chemical, or biological. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the process of freezing and expanding of water?\n2. How does this process affect rocks?\n3. Is this process a form of physical, chemical, or biological weathering?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The process of freezing and expanding of water occurs when water seeps into the cracks of rocks and freezes. When water freezes, it expands and puts pressure on the surrounding rock, causing it to crack and break apart.\n2. This process affects rocks by breaking them down into smaller pieces, which can eventually lead to the formation of soil.\n3. This process is a form of physical weathering, as it is caused by the physical force of water expanding as it freezes. \n\nTherefore, the answer is A) weathering.",
