                    {
                        "id": "ab84ce02-eac4-4d87-a4b5-8d16831ce35a",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which weather event is most likely to cause a forest fire, we need to consider the factors that contribute to the ignition and spread of fires in forested areas. Forest fires typically start when there is a source of heat, dry vegetation, and oxygen. Weather events can play a role in creating these conditions or directly igniting fires.\n\nA) A flash flood is a sudden, localized flood typically caused by heavy rainfall. While it can cause damage to vegetation and soil, it is unlikely to cause a forest fire as it involves an excess of water, which would dampen the vegetation and reduce the risk of ignition.\n\nB) A lightning strike is a discharge of electricity from the atmosphere, typically during a thunderstorm. Lightning can generate intense heat, reaching temperatures of around 30,000 Kelvin (54,000 degrees Fahrenheit). This heat can ignite dry vegetation and start a forest fire.\n\nC) A tornado is a rapidly rotating column of air that forms during severe thunderstorms. While tornadoes can cause significant damage to forests by uprooting trees and scattering debris, they are not typically associated with the ignition of forest fires. The high winds may help spread an existing fire, but they are not a direct cause.\n\nD) A hailstorm is a weather event characterized by the formation of ice pellets (hail) that fall from the sky. Hailstorms can cause damage to vegetation and structures, but they do not generate the heat necessary to ignite a forest fire.\n\nBased on this analysis, the weather event most likely to cause a forest fire is:\n\nB) a lightning strike",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f9f3ff7c-6879-44d1-8268-92d636f9276d",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) a lightning strike.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
