                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definition of each weather event.\n\nA flash flood is a rapid rise in water levels in a short period of time, usually caused by heavy rainfall.\n\nA lightning strike is a sudden and powerful electrical discharge from the atmosphere to the ground.\n\nA tornado is a rapidly rotating column of air that is in contact with both the surface of the Earth and a cumulonimbus cloud.\n\nA hailstorm is a storm characterized by the presence of large hailstones.\n\nStep 2: Consider which weather event is most likely to cause a forest fire.\n\nA lightning strike is the most likely weather event to cause a forest fire. Lightning strikes can cause fires by igniting dry vegetation, and they are more common in areas with high temperatures and low humidity.\n\nAnswer: B) a lightning strike",
                        "answers": [
