                        "cot": "\nStudent: Which weather event is most likely to cause a forest fire?\n\nProfessor: That's a great question. The answer is B) a lightning strike. Lightning is a common cause of forest fires because it can ignite dry vegetation and start a fire.\n\nStudent: How does lightning start a fire?\n\nProfessor: Lightning is a spark of electricity that can heat up the air around it to temperatures of up to 30,000 degrees Celsius. This heat can ignite dry vegetation, which can then spread and cause a forest fire.",
