                    {
                        "id": "b4bcfd69-4104-43ca-842f-fdc55e82aed2",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to understand what gravitational energy is and how it can be used to generate electricity.\n\nGravitational energy is the potential energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field. In the case of alternative energy resources, we are interested in the gravitational energy of water.\n\nHydropower is a form of energy that uses the gravitational energy of water to generate electricity. This is done by building a dam across a river or other body of water, creating a reservoir of water behind the dam. When the water is released, it flows through turbines, which spin generators to produce electricity.\n\nTidal energy is another form of energy that uses the gravitational energy of water to generate electricity. This is done by building a barrage or other structure across a tidal estuary or bay. When the tide comes in, the water is trapped behind the barrage, creating a difference in water level between the two sides. When the tide goes out, the water flows through turbines, which spin generators to produce electricity.\n\nGeothermal energy and wind energy do not use gravitational energy to generate electricity. Geothermal energy is generated by the heat of the Earth's core, while wind energy is generated by the kinetic energy of moving air.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f96377e4-0b3d-4bfd-81c9-adeb672c1e46",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) tidal energy and hydropower.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
