                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to understand what gravitational energy is and how it is used to make electricity. Gravitational energy is the energy stored in an object due to its position in a gravitational field. This energy can be released when the object is moved, and it can be used to do work, such as generating electricity.\n\nTidal energy and hydropower are two alternative energy resources that use gravitational energy to generate electricity. Tidal energy is generated by the gravitational pull of the moon and sun on the Earth's oceans, which causes the tides to rise and fall. This movement of water can be used to turn turbines and generate electricity. Hydropower is generated by the gravitational force of falling water, which is used to turn turbines and generate electricity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) tidal energy and hydropower.",
