                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) reflected.\n\nExplanation: When light hits a mirror, the majority of the light is reflected off the surface of the mirror. This is because the surface of the mirror is smooth and flat, which causes the light to bounce off the surface in the same direction it came from. This is known as reflection. Refraction occurs when light passes through a medium, such as glass or water, and is bent as it passes through. Absorption occurs when light is absorbed by a material, such as a black surface. Transmission occurs when light passes through a medium, such as air or glass, without being bent or absorbed.",
