                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question and the given information. We know that both sound waves have the same pitch, but the second one is louder.\n\nStep 2: Recall the properties of sound waves. Sound waves have properties such as frequency, amplitude, wavelength, and speed in air.\n\nStep 3: Relate the given information to the properties of sound waves. The pitch of a sound wave is related to its frequency, and the loudness of a sound wave is related to its amplitude.\n\nStep 4: Compare the properties of the two sound waves. Since both sound waves have the same pitch, their frequencies are the same. However, the second sound wave is louder, which means it has a greater amplitude.\n\nStep 5: Choose the correct answer based on the comparison. The property that is greater for the second sound wave is amplitude.\n\nAnswer: B) Amplitude",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "26c3b88f-5e79-49f0-baa9-897d54a3b59c",
