                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: A person plays a flute and creates two sound waves one after the other. Both waves have the same pitch, but the second one is louder. Which property is greater for the second sound wave?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\n1. We know that both sound waves have the same pitch. Pitch is determined by the frequency of a sound wave, so both waves have the same frequency.\n\n2. The second sound wave is louder than the first one. Loudness is determined by the amplitude of a sound wave. Therefore, the second sound wave must have a greater amplitude.\n\n3. Wavelength and speed in air are not directly related to the loudness of a sound wave, so we can rule out these options.\n\nBased on our reasoning, the correct answer is B) Amplitude. The second sound wave has a greater amplitude, which makes it louder than the first sound wave.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "08623750-a22f-4d40-a14e-73cf50d12e3a",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Amplitude.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
