                    {
                        "id": "640bba14-bb1a-4e5b-a63a-b2386c2d1227",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Which of the following properties is greater for the second sound wave?\nA) Frequency\nB) Amplitude\nC) Wavelength\nD) Speed in air\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n- Sound waves are mechanical waves that propagate through a medium (such as air) due to the vibration of particles.\n- The pitch of a sound wave is determined by its frequency, which is the number of oscillations (vibrations) per unit of time.\n- The loudness of a sound wave is determined by its amplitude, which is the maximum displacement of particles from their equilibrium position during one oscillation.\n- The wavelength of a sound wave is the distance between two consecutive points in the same phase of the wave (e.g., two consecutive compressions or rarefactions).\n- The speed of a sound wave in a medium depends on the properties of the medium (e.g., temperature, pressure, and density) and is generally constant for a given medium under specific conditions.\n\nSub-questions and answers:\n1) Do the two sound waves have the same frequency?\nYes, since both sound waves have the same pitch, they have the same frequency.\n\n2) Do the two sound waves have the same amplitude?\nNo, since the second sound wave is louder, it has a greater amplitude.\n\n3) Do the two sound waves have the same wavelength?\nYes, since both sound waves have the same frequency and speed in air, they have the same wavelength.\n\n4) Do the two sound waves have the same speed in air?\nYes, since the speed of sound in air depends on the properties of the medium and not on the properties of the sound wave itself, both sound waves have the same speed in air.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nThe property that is greater for the second sound wave is B) Amplitude.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a6276c47-9e55-40eb-a54f-562a374725f4",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Amplitude.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 07:46:41",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
