                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nB) Amplitude\n\nThe pitch of a sound wave is determined by its frequency, which is the number of complete cycles of the waveform per second. The amplitude of a sound wave is determined by its loudness, which is the maximum displacement of the waveform from its equilibrium position. Therefore, if the second sound wave is louder, its amplitude must be greater than the first sound wave.",
