                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the function of the digestive system.\n2. Read through the options and eliminate those that do not match the identified function.\n3. Choose the option that matches the identified function.\n\nAnswer: \n1. The function of the digestive system is to break down food into nutrients that can be absorbed by the body.\n2. A) carrying oxygen to the lungs is a function of the respiratory system, not the digestive system. B) sending signals from the brain to the spinal cord is a function of the nervous system, not the digestive system. D) providing support for the body is a function of the skeletal system, not the digestive system.\n3. Therefore, the correct answer is C) breaking down food into nutrients.",
