                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) breaking down food into nutrients.\n\nExplanation:\nThe digestive system is responsible for breaking down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed and used by the body. This process involves mechanical and chemical digestion in various organs such as the mouth, stomach, small intestine, and large intestine. The nutrients obtained from food are then transported to the cells of the body for energy, growth, and repair. Therefore, option C is the correct answer. \n\nOption A is incorrect because carrying oxygen to the lungs is the function of the respiratory system, which includes the lungs, trachea, bronchi, and other structures involved in breathing. \n\nOption B is incorrect because sending signals from the brain to the spinal cord is the function of the nervous system, which includes the brain, spinal cord, and nerves that transmit messages throughout the body. \n\nOption D is incorrect because providing support for the body is the function of the skeletal system, which includes bones, cartilage, and other connective tissues that provide structure and protection for the body.",
