                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what a function is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, a function is a specific purpose or role that something serves.\n\nStudent: Okay, got it. So, which of the options is a function of the digestive system?\n\nProfessor: The function of the digestive system is to break down food into nutrients. So, the answer is C.\n\nStudent: How does the digestive system break down food into nutrients?\n\nProfessor: The digestive system uses enzymes to break down food into smaller molecules that can be absorbed by the body. These molecules are then transported to the cells where they are used for energy and other functions.\n\nStudent: What happens to the food that is not broken down into nutrients?\n\nProfessor: The food that is not broken down into nutrients is eliminated from the body as waste.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor. I understand now.",
