                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand the function of the digestive system in the human body. The digestive system is responsible for breaking down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body for energy, growth, and cell repair.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) carrying oxygen to the lungs - This is not a function of the digestive system. This is a function of the respiratory system, which is responsible for exchanging oxygen and carbon dioxide between the body and the environment.\n\nB) sending signals from the brain to the spinal cord - This is not a function of the digestive system. This is a function of the nervous system, which is responsible for transmitting signals between different parts of the body, including the brain and spinal cord.\n\nC) breaking down food into nutrients - This is a function of the digestive system, as mentioned earlier. The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body.\n\nD) providing support for the body - This is not a function of the digestive system. This is a function of the skeletal system, which is responsible for providing support and protection for the body's organs.\n\nBased on the analysis above, the correct answer is:\n\nC) breaking down food into nutrients",
