                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure which option is the correct function of the digestive system. Can you help me understand each option better?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option one by one. Option A is \"carrying oxygen to the lungs.\" This is actually a function of the respiratory system, not the digestive system. The respiratory system is responsible for exchanging oxygen and carbon dioxide between the body and the environment.\n\nStudent: Okay, so option A is not the correct answer. What about option B?\n\nProfessor: Option B is \"sending signals from the brain to the spinal cord.\" This is a function of the nervous system. The nervous system is responsible for transmitting signals throughout the body, allowing us to move, think, and sense our surroundings.\n\nStudent: I see. So option B is also not the correct answer. How about option C?\n\nProfessor: Option C is \"breaking down food into nutrients.\" This is indeed a function of the digestive system. The digestive system is responsible for breaking down the food we eat into smaller molecules that our body can absorb and use for energy, growth, and repair.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. So option C is the correct answer. But can you explain option D as well?\n\nProfessor: Sure! Option D is \"providing support for the body.\" This is a function of the skeletal system. The skeletal system is made up of bones, which provide support and protection for our organs and allow us to move.\n\nStudent: So the correct answer is option C, \"breaking down food into nutrients,\" because that is the function of the digestive system. Thank you for explaining each option to me!\n\nProfessor: You're welcome! I'm glad I could help you understand the functions of the different systems in the human body.",
