                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain the question again?\n\nProfessor: Sure. The question is asking where in a plant you would find the most parts that capture sunlight to make food.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what are these parts called?\n\nProfessor: They are called chloroplasts.\n\nStudent: And what do they do?\n\nProfessor: Chloroplasts capture sunlight and use it to make food for the plant through a process called photosynthesis.\n\nStudent: Got it. So, where in the plant would you find the most chloroplasts?\n\nProfessor: The answer is C) leaves. Leaves are the primary site of photosynthesis in a plant and contain the most chloroplasts.\n\nStudent: Why not the flowers?\n\nProfessor: While flowers do contain chloroplasts, they are not the primary site of photosynthesis in a plant. Their main function is to attract pollinators for reproduction.\n\nStudent: And what about the roots and stems?\n\nProfessor: Roots and stems do not contain chloroplasts at all. They have other important functions in the plant, such as absorbing water and nutrients from the soil and providing support for the plant.",
