                    {
                        "id": "f05068f7-f8c3-4ac0-b17f-cb8b153c7076",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: In which part of a plant are the most specialized structures for capturing sunlight and producing food located?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\n1. We know that plants use a process called photosynthesis to convert sunlight into food.\n2. Photosynthesis occurs in specialized structures called chloroplasts, which contain chlorophyll, the pigment responsible for capturing sunlight.\n3. Different parts of a plant have different functions, so we need to determine which part contains the most chloroplasts.\n4. Roots are responsible for absorbing water and nutrients from the soil, so they are not the primary location for photosynthesis.\n5. Stems provide support and transport nutrients and water throughout the plant, but they also do not contain a high concentration of chloroplasts.\n6. Leaves are the primary site of photosynthesis in most plants, as they have a large surface area exposed to sunlight and contain a high concentration of chloroplasts.\n7. Flowers are involved in reproduction and may contain some chloroplasts, but their primary function is not photosynthesis.\n\nBased on this reasoning, the correct answer is:\n\nC) leaves",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "1790c981-1a62-4f1f-80f5-02bb102c6f54",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) leaves, as they contain the most specialized structures for capturing sunlight and producing food in a plant.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/13 07:57:46",
