                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe most of these parts in a plant can be found in leaves. This is because leaves are the primary organ for photosynthesis, which is the process of using sunlight to make food. Leaves contain chloroplasts, which are the organelles that contain the chlorophyll that captures the sunlight. The leaves also contain other organelles such as mitochondria and endoplasmic reticulum that are necessary for photosynthesis. Therefore, the answer is C) leaves.",
                        "answers": [
