                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nComplementary Knowledge:\nPlant cells use special parts called chloroplasts to capture sunlight. Chloroplasts use the energy from the sunlight to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose, a type of sugar, through a process called photosynthesis.\n\nSub-Questions:\n1. Where are chloroplasts located in a plant?\n2. What parts of a plant are most exposed to sunlight?\n\nAnswer:\n1. Chloroplasts are located in the cells of a plant's leaves, stems, and flowers.\n2. Leaves are the most exposed to sunlight, so they will have the most chloroplasts.\n\nAnswer: C) leaves",
                        "answers": [
