                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Energy and nutrients are essential for the human body to function properly. Energy is required for physical activity and to maintain bodily functions, while nutrients are necessary for growth, repair, and maintenance of tissues.\n\nAdditional facts: The human body requires a variety of nutrients, including carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, and minerals. These nutrients are obtained through the food we eat and are broken down and absorbed by the body's digestive system.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the different types of nutrients required by the human body?\n2. How does the body break down and absorb nutrients from food?\n3. What are the sources of food that provide the necessary nutrients?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The human body requires carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, and minerals to function properly.\n2. The digestive system breaks down food into smaller molecules, which are then absorbed into the bloodstream and transported to cells throughout the body.\n3. Food sources that provide necessary nutrients include fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and healthy fats.\n\nAnswer to original question: People get energy and nutrients by eating healthy food that provides the necessary carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, and minerals required by the body.",
                        "answers": [
