                    {
                        "id": "e42551ff-bbf7-4751-a3f6-f34ec7eef40d",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the first-level consumer, we need to understand the different levels of consumers in a food chain.\n\nA food chain is a linear sequence of organisms through which nutrients and energy pass as one organism eats another. The levels in a food chain are called trophic levels, and they represent the position an organism occupies in the food chain.\n\nThere are three main types of consumers in a food chain:\n\n1. Primary consumers (first-level consumers): These are organisms that eat producers (plants). They are also known as herbivores.\n\n2. Secondary consumers (second-level consumers): These are organisms that eat primary consumers. They are also known as carnivores or predators.\n\n3. Tertiary consumers (third-level consumers): These are organisms that eat secondary consumers. They are also known as top predators.\n\nNow let's analyze the given options:\n\nA) Wolf: A wolf is a carnivore that eats other animals, such as deer or rabbits. Therefore, it is a secondary consumer.\n\nB) Hawk: A hawk is a carnivore that eats other animals, such as rodents or smaller birds. Therefore, it is a secondary or tertiary consumer.\n\nC) Carrot: A carrot is a plant, which is a producer in the food chain. It is not a consumer.\n\nD) Rabbit: A rabbit is an herbivore that eats plants, such as grass or vegetables. Therefore, it is a primary consumer (first-level consumer).\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Rabbit",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "cb008c0f-3e9e-4096-8e9d-9c418d688412",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Rabbit, as it is a primary consumer (first-level consumer) that eats plants, such as grass or vegetables.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
