                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I have a question. What does Jessica want to see in an oak tree leaf?\n\nProfessor: Jessica wants to see the cells in an oak tree leaf.\n\nStudent: Okay, and what is the best tool for her to use to see the cells?\n\nProfessor: The best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells is a microscope.\n\nStudent: Why is a microscope the best tool?\n\nProfessor: A microscope is the best tool because it can magnify the cells to a level that is visible to the human eye. It can also provide a clear image of the cells.\n\nStudent: Can she use a magnifying glass instead of a microscope?\n\nProfessor: A magnifying glass can be used, but it may not provide a clear image of the cells. It also may not magnify the cells to a level that is visible to the human eye.\n\nStudent: What about binoculars or reading glasses?\n\nProfessor: Binoculars and reading glasses are not suitable for seeing cells in an oak tree leaf. They are designed for different purposes and cannot magnify the cells to a level that is visible to the human eye.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor. I understand now that a microscope is the best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf.",
