                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf, we need to consider the size of the cells and the magnification capabilities of each tool.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n- Plant cells are typically between 10 and 100 micrometers in size.\n- Binoculars are designed for viewing distant objects and typically have a magnification of 7x to 10x.\n- Microscopes are designed for viewing small objects at high magnification, typically ranging from 40x to 1000x or more.\n- Reading glasses are designed to help people with presbyopia (age-related difficulty in focusing on near objects) and typically have a magnification of 1x to 3x.\n- Magnifying glasses are handheld lenses that can magnify objects, typically with a magnification of 2x to 20x.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) Which tools have a magnification range suitable for viewing plant cells?\n2) Which tool is specifically designed for viewing small objects at high magnification?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1) Microscopes and magnifying glasses have a magnification range suitable for viewing plant cells.\n2) Microscopes are specifically designed for viewing small objects at high magnification.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nThe best tool for Jessica to use to see the cells in an oak tree leaf is a microscope (option B).",
