                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain the question again, please?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Robert added an indicator to vinegar, and the color turned red. Then he added drops of ammonia solution until the color disappeared. The question is asking what process occurred during this experiment.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand. So, what is an indicator?\n\nProfessor: An indicator is a substance that changes color when it comes into contact with an acid or a base.\n\nStudent: Got it. And what is vinegar?\n\nProfessor: Vinegar is an acid. It contains acetic acid.\n\nStudent: And what about ammonia solution?\n\nProfessor: Ammonia solution is a base. It contains ammonia.\n\nStudent: So, what happened when Robert added the indicator to vinegar?\n\nProfessor: The indicator changed color, indicating that the vinegar was an acid.\n\nStudent: And what happened when he added drops of ammonia solution?\n\nProfessor: The color disappeared, indicating that the vinegar and ammonia had reacted with each other.\n\nStudent: So, what process occurred during this experiment?\n\nProfessor: The process that occurred is called neutralization. The acid (vinegar) and base (ammonia) reacted with each other to form a neutral solution.",
