                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand the properties of the substances involved and the possible chemical reactions that can occur between them.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. Vinegar is a weak acid, primarily composed of acetic acid (CH3COOH).\n2. An indicator is a substance that changes color depending on the pH of the solution it is in. In this case, the indicator turns red in acidic solutions.\n3. Ammonia solution, also known as ammonium hydroxide (NH4OH), is a weak base.\n4. Neutralization is a chemical reaction between an acid and a base, resulting in the formation of a salt and water.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens when an acid reacts with a base?\nAnswer: When an acid reacts with a base, a neutralization reaction occurs, producing a salt and water.\n\n2. What is the reaction between acetic acid and ammonium hydroxide?\nAnswer: The reaction between acetic acid (CH3COOH) and ammonium hydroxide (NH4OH) is a neutralization reaction, resulting in the formation of ammonium acetate (NH4CH3COO) and water (H2O).\n\nOriginal question: What process occurred when Robert added ammonia solution to vinegar until the color disappeared?\nAnswer: D) neutralization",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3192db19-8844-496f-8c94-a82f99d9dfea",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) neutralization. The process that occurred when Robert added ammonia solution to vinegar until the color disappeared was a neutralization reaction between the acetic acid in the vinegar and the ammonium hydroxide in the ammonia solution, resulting in the formation of ammonium acetate and water.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
