                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the process of melting.\n2. Determine what happens to the temperature of the ice cube when it is set out in a warm room.\n3. Determine what happens to the temperature of the air in the room.\n4. Determine how heat is transferred.\n5. Choose the statement that best describes the reason why the ice cube melts.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Melting is the process of changing a solid into a liquid.\n2. When the ice cube is set out in a warm room, the temperature of the ice cube increases.\n3. The temperature of the air in the room also increases.\n4. Heat is transferred from warmer objects to cooler objects through conduction, convection, or radiation.\n5. The statement that best describes the reason why the ice cube melts when set out in a warm room is A) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.",
