                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is A) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.\n\nWhen an ice cube is set out in a warm room, the temperature of the room is higher than the temperature of the ice cube. Heat always flows from a warmer object to a cooler object. Therefore, heat from the room is transferred to the ice cube. As the ice cube absorbs heat, its molecules gain energy and begin to move faster. This causes the ice cube to melt and turn into liquid water. Therefore, option A is the correct statement that describes the reason why an ice cube melts when set out in a warm room. Option B is incorrect because the molecules of the ice cube actually move faster as they absorb heat. Option C is incorrect because the temperature of the ice cube is uniform throughout. Option D is incorrect because heat from the ice cube is actually moving into the ice cube, not into the air.",
