                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain why an ice cube melts when set out in a warm room?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Which answer choice do you think is correct?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. Can you explain each option?\n\nProfessor: Of course. Option A says that heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube. This is correct because heat always flows from warmer objects to cooler objects. So, when the ice cube is in a warm room, heat from the room is transferred to the ice cube, causing it to melt.\n\nStudent: Okay, that makes sense. What about option B?\n\nProfessor: Option B says that the ice cube molecules move more slowly. This is not correct because when an object is heated, its molecules move faster, not slower. So, this option is not the reason why an ice cube melts in a warm room.\n\nStudent: I see. What about option C?\n\nProfessor: Option C says that one side of the ice cube is colder than the other. This is not correct because the temperature of an object is the same throughout, unless there is a temperature gradient. In the case of an ice cube in a warm room, the temperature of the ice cube is uniform, so this option is not the reason why it melts.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand. What about option D?\n\nProfessor: Option D says that heat from the ice cube moves into the air. This is also correct because heat always flows from warmer objects to cooler objects. So, when the ice cube is in a warm room, heat from the ice cube is transferred to the air, causing the ice cube to melt.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that to me. I understand now.",
