                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the correct answer, let's analyze each statement:\n\nA) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.\n- This statement suggests that the warmer temperature in the room is causing the ice cube to absorb heat, which could lead to melting.\n\nB) The ice cube molecules move more slowly.\n- This statement is incorrect because when ice melts, its molecules actually move faster due to the increased energy from the heat.\n\nC) One side of the ice cube is colder than the other.\n- This statement is irrelevant to the reason why an ice cube melts in a warm room. The overall temperature of the room is what affects the ice cube, not just one side of it.\n\nD) Heat from the ice cube moves into the air.\n- This statement is incorrect because it suggests that the ice cube is losing heat to the air, which would cause it to become colder, not melt.\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nA) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.\n\nWhen an ice cube is set out in a warm room, the heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube, causing its molecules to move faster and change from a solid state (ice) to a liquid state (water). This is the reason why an ice cube melts when set out in a warm room.",
