                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand the process of melting and the role of heat in this process. Melting is a phase transition from a solid to a liquid state, which occurs when a substance absorbs enough heat to overcome the forces holding its molecules together in a rigid structure.\n\nNow, let's address each statement and determine which one accurately describes the reason why an ice cube melts when set out in a warm room.\n\nA) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.\nThis statement suggests that the ice cube absorbs heat from the surrounding environment, which could cause the ice cube to melt. This is a plausible explanation, as heat transfer from a warmer environment to a colder object is a fundamental principle of thermodynamics.\n\nB) The ice cube molecules move more slowly.\nThis statement is incorrect because, as a substance absorbs heat, its molecules generally move faster, not slower. In the case of an ice cube, as it absorbs heat, the water molecules gain kinetic energy and move more rapidly, eventually breaking the bonds that hold them in a solid structure.\n\nC) One side of the ice cube is colder than the other.\nThis statement does not explain why an ice cube melts in a warm room. While it is possible that one side of the ice cube may be colder than the other, this does not provide a reason for the overall melting process.\n\nD) Heat from the ice cube moves into the air.\nThis statement is also incorrect. In a warm room, the air is warmer than the ice cube, so heat would transfer from the air to the ice cube, not the other way around.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct statement is:\n\nA) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.\n\nThis statement accurately describes the reason why an ice cube melts when set out in a warm room. The ice cube absorbs heat from the warmer surrounding environment, causing its molecules to gain kinetic energy and break the bonds holding them in a solid structure, resulting in the melting process.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "5785bbd5-4d64-4a5f-bef2-1f702a848bab",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Heat from the room is absorbed by the ice cube.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": true
