                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the definitions of each of the terms.\nA) Solute: A substance that is dissolved in a solution.\nB) Solvent: A liquid in which a solute is dissolved.\nC) Solution: A mixture of two or more substances in which the molecules of the solute are evenly distributed throughout the solvent.\nD) Suspension: A mixture of two or more substances in which the molecules of the solute are not evenly distributed throughout the solvent.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the given information.\nThe student has dissolved a spoonful of sugar in a glass of water.\n\nStep 3: Determine the answer.\nThe answer is C) Solution. The student has dissolved a spoonful of sugar in a glass of water, which means that the molecules of the solute (sugar) are evenly distributed throughout the solvent (water), making it a solution.",
