                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking why electrical wires are coated with rubber or plastic. To answer this question, we need to understand the properties of rubber and plastic in relation to electricity.\n\nRubber and plastic are both good insulators. This means that they do not conduct electricity well. In fact, they have very high resistance to the flow of electrical current. This is why they are used to coat electrical wires.\n\nWhen an electrical current flows through a wire, it generates heat. If the wire is not insulated, this heat can escape into the surrounding environment, which can be dangerous. Additionally, if the wire comes into contact with other conductive materials, it can cause a short circuit, which can also be dangerous.\n\nBy coating the wire with rubber or plastic, we can prevent these problems. The insulation provides a barrier that prevents the electrical current from escaping and coming into contact with other materials. This makes the wire safer to use and reduces the risk of electrical fires or other hazards.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) insulators.",
                        "answers": [
