                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Why are electrical wires coated with rubber or plastic?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Electrical wires are used to transmit electricity from one point to another.\n- However, if the wire is not coated, the electricity can leak out or cause harm to people or objects it comes into contact with.\n- Therefore, the wire needs to be coated with a material that can prevent the electricity from escaping or causing harm.\n- Rubber and plastic are commonly used materials for this purpose.\n- These materials are good at preventing the flow of electricity, which makes them good insulators.\n- Therefore, the answer is C) insulators.\n\nAnswer: C) insulators.",
                        "answers": [
