                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain why electrical wires are coated with rubber or plastic?\n\nProfessor: Sure, electrical wires are coated with rubber or plastic because these materials are good what?\n\nStudent: Um, I'm not sure. Can you give me the options again?\n\nProfessor: Of course. Are they good resistors, magnets, insulators, or conductors?\n\nStudent: Oh, right. They are good insulators, aren't they?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Rubber and plastic are good insulators because they do not allow electricity to flow through them easily. This is important because if the electricity were to flow through the wire and into something it's not supposed to, it could cause damage or even be dangerous.\n\nStudent: I see. So, why do we need electrical wires to conduct electricity in the first place?\n\nProfessor: Good question. Electrical wires are used to conduct electricity because they are made of materials that allow electricity to flow through them easily. These materials are called conductors, and they include things like copper and aluminum. By using these materials, we can create a path for the electricity to flow from one place to another, such as from a power plant to our homes.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. Thank you for explaining it to me, professor.\n\nProfessor: You're welcome. Do you have any other questions?",
