                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the purpose of coating electrical wires.\n- The coating on electrical wires is meant to prevent the flow of electricity from the wire to other objects or people, ensuring safety and proper functioning of the electrical system.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the given options.\n- A) Resistors: These are components that reduce the flow of electric current, but they still allow some current to pass through.\n- B) Magnets: These are objects that produce a magnetic field, which is not related to the purpose of coating electrical wires.\n- C) Insulators: These are materials that do not allow the flow of electric current, providing protection and safety.\n- D) Conductors: These are materials that allow the flow of electric current, which is the opposite of what we need for coating electrical wires.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct option based on the analysis.\n- The correct answer is C) Insulators, as they prevent the flow of electric current and provide safety and proper functioning of the electrical system.",
