                    {
                        "id": "d4e54b57-a28a-4b49-9b4b-f27ae9f6ece3",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand the purpose of coating electrical wires with rubber or plastic.\n\nThe coating on electrical wires serves as a protective layer to prevent electrical current from escaping the wire and causing short circuits, shocks, or other hazards. Therefore, the material used for coating should not allow electricity to pass through it easily.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Resistors: Resistors are components in electrical circuits that reduce the flow of electrical current. While they do limit the flow of electricity, they still allow some current to pass through. So, this is not the best answer.\n\nB) Magnets: Magnets produce a magnetic field and can attract or repel certain materials, but they do not have any direct effect on the flow of electrical current. Therefore, this option is not correct.\n\nC) Insulators: Insulators are materials that do not allow electricity to pass through them easily. They are used to prevent the flow of electrical current and protect against electrical hazards. This seems like the correct answer, but let's check the last option as well.\n\nD) Conductors: Conductors are materials that allow electricity to flow through them easily. Using a conductor as a coating for electrical wires would defeat the purpose of the protective layer, as it would allow the electrical current to escape. So, this option is not correct.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Insulators.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "fb0f389f-e55b-43b5-a233-6f7b5660eebc",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Insulators. Electrical wires are coated with rubber or plastic because these materials are good insulators, preventing electrical current from escaping the wire and causing short circuits, shocks, or other hazards.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
