                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA) Resistors\n\nExplanation: Electrical wires are coated with a rubber or plastic because these materials are good insulators, meaning they do not allow electricity to pass through them. Insulators are the opposite of conductors, which allow electricity to pass through them. Resistors are components that are used to control the flow of electricity in a circuit, and magnets are not related to the insulation of electrical wires. Therefore, the correct answer is A) Resistors.",
