                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStudent: What is the purpose of coating electrical wires with rubber or plastic?\n\nProfessor: The purpose of coating electrical wires with rubber or plastic is to provide insulation. These materials are good insulators, which means they don't allow electricity to pass through them. This prevents the wires from shorting out and causing electrical fires.\n\nStudent: So, why are insulators used instead of conductors?\n\nProfessor: Insulators are used instead of conductors because conductors allow electricity to pass through them, which would be dangerous in this situation. Insulators, on the other hand, prevent electricity from passing through them, which is why they are used to coat electrical wires.\n\nStudent: So, the correct answer is C) insulators?\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Insulators are the best choice for coating electrical wires because they prevent electricity from passing through them.",
