                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Chemical properties describe how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is density?\n2. Is density a property that describes how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances?\n3. What is flammability?\n4. Is flammability a property that describes how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances?\n5. What is color?\n6. Is color a property that describes how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances?\n7. What is brittleness?\n8. Is brittleness a property that describes how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Density is the amount of mass per unit volume of a substance.\n2. No, density is a physical property that describes the amount of matter in a given space.\n3. Flammability is the ability of a substance to burn or ignite when exposed to a flame or spark.\n4. Yes, flammability is a chemical property because it describes how a substance reacts with oxygen in the air to form new substances (such as carbon dioxide and water) when it burns.\n5. Color is the visual appearance of a substance due to the way it reflects or absorbs light.\n6. No, color is a physical property that does not describe how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances.\n7. Brittleness is the tendency of a substance to break or shatter when subjected to stress or pressure.\n8. No, brittleness is a physical property that does not describe how a substance interacts with other substances to form new substances.",
