                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: Which of these is a chemical property of a material?\nA) density\nB) flammability\nC) color\nD) brittleness\n\nAnswer: B) flammability\n\nExplanation: A chemical property of a material is a property that describes how a material reacts with other substances. Density, color, and brittleness are all physical properties, which describe the physical characteristics of a material, such as its size, shape, and texture. Flammability, on the other hand, is a chemical property, which describes how easily a material can be set on fire. Therefore, the correct answer is B) flammability.",
