l depend on factors like the temperature and the amount of heat applied, as well as the mass of the samples. Since the masses are different, it's unlikely that the time required for the changes will be the same. So, option D is not correct.\n\nStudent: So, the correct answer is option C, both groups will have the same mass with which they started.\n\nProfessor",
