                    {
                        "id": "59a6302e-4f98-4a25-b776-9422e2d13694",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the correct answer, let's analyze each option in relation to the purpose of refrigerators:\n\nA) Growing food: Refrigerators do not contribute to the growth of food, as they are used for preserving food after it has been harvested or prepared. So, this option is not correct.\n\nB) Cleaning food: Refrigerators do not clean food. Cleaning food is typically done by washing it with water before storing it in the refrigerator. So, this option is not correct.\n\nC) Keeping food dry: While refrigerators can help maintain a certain level of humidity, their primary purpose is not to keep food dry. Some foods may even become more moist in a refrigerator due to condensation. So, this option is not correct.\n\nD) Keeping food fresh: Refrigerators were invented to keep food cold, which slows down the growth of bacteria and other microorganisms that cause food to spoil. By doing this, refrigerators help to keep food fresh for a longer period of time. So, this option is correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) keeping food fresh.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "12256c94-bc13-4708-81d5-2f64565a1d8b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
