                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure which option is correct. Can you help me understand how refrigerators help with food?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option step by step. First, do you think refrigerators help in growing food?\n\nStudent: No, I don't think so. Growing food happens before it reaches the refrigerator.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. Now, what about cleaning food? Do refrigerators help with that?\n\nStudent: I don't think so either. We usually clean food before putting it in the refrigerator.\n\nProfessor: Right again. Now, let's consider option C, keeping food dry. Do you think refrigerators help with that?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. I know refrigerators are cold, but I don't know if they keep food dry.\n\nProfessor: Good question. Refrigerators do help to some extent in keeping food dry by controlling humidity, but their primary function is not to keep food dry. So, let's move on to the last option, keeping food fresh. What do you think about that?\n\nStudent: That makes sense to me. Refrigerators keep food cold, which can slow down the growth of bacteria and help food stay fresh longer.\n\nProfessor: Exactly! So, based on our discussion, which option do you think is the correct answer?\n\nStudent: I think the correct answer is D) keeping food fresh.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! Well done. By going through each option step by step, you were able to understand the primary function of refrigerators and arrive at the right answer.",
