                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) dependent variables are most likely placed along the y-axis. \n\nThe y-axis is typically used to represent the dependent variable in a graph. The dependent variable is the variable that is being measured or observed and is affected by the independent variable. For example, in a graph showing the relationship between time and distance traveled, time would be placed on the x-axis (independent variable) and distance traveled would be placed on the y-axis (dependent variable). \n\nOption A, element symbols, is not typically placed on the y-axis as they are not related to the variables being graphed. \n\nOption B, negative numbers, may be placed on the y-axis if the dependent variable can have negative values, but it is not the most likely option. \n\nOption D, independent variables, are typically placed on the x-axis as they are the variable being manipulated or controlled in the experiment. \n\nTherefore, the most likely option to be placed along the y-axis is C) dependent variables.",
