                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question and what is being asked. The question is asking what is most likely placed along the y-axis on a graph.\n\nStep 2: Recall the basic structure of a graph. A graph typically has two axes: the x-axis (horizontal) and the y-axis (vertical).\n\nStep 3: Recall the purpose of each axis. The x-axis usually represents the independent variable, while the y-axis represents the dependent variable. The dependent variable is the one that changes in response to the independent variable.\n\nStep 4: Evaluate the given options based on the information from Step 3.\n\nA) Element symbols: This is not a typical representation for the y-axis, as element symbols are not dependent variables.\n\nB) Negative numbers: While negative numbers can be present on the y-axis, they are not the primary purpose of the y-axis.\n\nC) Dependent variables: This is the correct answer, as the y-axis typically represents the dependent variable.\n\nD) Independent variables: This is incorrect, as the x-axis typically represents the independent variable.\n\nAnswer: C) Dependent variables",
