                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine what is most likely placed along the y-axis, let's first understand the purpose of the y-axis and its relationship with the x-axis (horizontal axis) on a graph.\n\nIn a graph, the x-axis typically represents the independent variable, which is the variable that is manipulated or controlled in an experiment or study. The y-axis, on the other hand, represents the dependent variable, which is the variable that is being measured or observed as a result of the changes in the independent variable.\n\nNow, let's analyze each of the given options:\n\nA) Element symbols: These are not typically placed along the y-axis, as they are not variables that can be measured or observed as a result of changes in another variable.\n\nB) Negative numbers: While the y-axis can include negative numbers, this option does not specifically refer to a type of variable that would be placed along the y-axis.\n\nC) Dependent variables: As mentioned earlier, the y-axis represents the dependent variable, which is the variable being measured or observed as a result of changes in the independent variable. This option aligns with the purpose of the y-axis.\n\nD) Independent variables: These are typically placed along the x-axis, not the y-axis.\n\nBased on the analysis, the most likely answer is:\n\nC) dependent variables",
