                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is C) dependent variables.\n\nThe y-axis on a graph is typically used to represent the dependent variable, which is the variable that is being measured or observed. The dependent variable is usually plotted on the y-axis because it is the variable that is affected by the independent variable, which is typically plotted on the x-axis. Therefore, the y-axis is most likely to contain the dependent variable.",
