                        "cot": "\nStudent: What is most likely placed along the y-axis?\n\nProfessor: The y-axis is the vertical axis on a graph. It is usually used to plot the dependent variable, which is the variable that changes in response to changes in the independent variable. So the answer to your question is C) dependent variables. \n\nStudent: So the dependent variable is the one that changes in response to changes in the independent variable?\n\nProfessor: That's right. The independent variable is the one that is changed to observe the effect on the dependent variable. For example, if you were studying the effect of temperature on the growth of a plant, the temperature would be the independent variable and the growth of the plant would be the dependent variable.",
